SAME-NAME COLLISION (disclosed in full)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two distinct web components share the name `RecentActivity`:
  • features/dashboard/components/RecentActivity.tsx  → P4/0130 (3 panels + battery chart).
  • features/vehicles/components/RecentActivity.tsx   → P4/0277 (THIS prompt; 2 panels, no chart).
The dashboard variant is already committed on disk as RecentActivity.* (11 files, types `RecentActivity*`),
with its own gate log p4-apple-feature-views-0130-RecentActivity.log. The monorepo Swift module is flat,
so top-level type names must be globally unique. Per the established precedent for these widget<->section
name collisions (see HEAD `fix(apps/apple): dedupe 2nd collision recurrence`), this vehicles variant ships
as `RecentActivity.Vehicles.*` files with a `VehiclesRecentActivity*` type namespace; the P-0130 dashboard
predecessor is left BYTE-IDENTICAL (git status clean on all 11 of its files). Both file stems match the
prompt's allowed glob `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentActivity.*`.

